3416 17592186045585 true] [17592186152580 1071 "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$y^{″}(x) + 4y(x) = 0, y(0) = y(1) = 0, 0 \\le x \\le 1$\n\nWhich of the following best classifies the boundary conditions for this problem?" 13194139533416 17592186045585 false] [17592186152580 1074 "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Periodic:\n\n$$\ny(a)=y(b),\\,{y}^{′}(a)={y}^{′}(b)\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following boundary conditions, defined on $x=a=0$ and $x=b=1.$\n\n$$\ny(0)=0,\\,y(1)=0\n$$\n\nThese are Dirichlet boundary conditions." 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186157460 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311585 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186157460 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311605 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186157460 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311607 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186157460 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311609 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186157461 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311831 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186157461 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311832 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186157461 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311833 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186157461 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311853 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186157461 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311854 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186157462 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311855 131