h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O({{{x}^{2}+3{x}^{3}}_{⏟}}_{f}).\n$$\n\nThis is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L3}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O({x}^{2}+3{x}^{3}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L2}$ we have\n\n$$\n3{x}^{3}=O({x}^{2})\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L2}$ and the $\\text{absorption property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O({x}^{2})\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line  $\\text{L3},$   we have\n\n$$\nf=O({x}^{2})\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0,\n$$\n\nand from line  $\\text{L4},$   we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=O(x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L3 and L4}$ and by $\\text{the transitive property},$  we conclude that\n\n$$\nf=O(x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$" 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311586 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311194 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311586 1069 "q-335376" 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311586 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [175921863