torname{cos}⁡(t)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)) & =\\frac{3}{25}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ (-\\alpha +4\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+(4\\alpha +\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & =\\frac{3}{25}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\alpha +4\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)) \\\\ 4\\alpha +\\beta =\\frac{3}{25}\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =\\frac{12}{425},\\beta =\\frac{3}{425}.$ Therefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{q}_{p}(t)=\\frac{12}{425}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\frac{3}{425}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\nq(t)={q}_{c}(t)+{q}_{p}(t)=A{e}^{-4t}+\\frac{12}{425}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\frac{3}{425}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $P=12,Q=3,$ and\n\n$$\nP+Q=12+3=15.\n$$" 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311813 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311017 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311813 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311075 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311813 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311255 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311813 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311266 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311813 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311360 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311813 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311362 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311813 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311424 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311813 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311482 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311813 1069 "q-337161" 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311813 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311813 1071 "Suppose we would like to find an int