}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) & =\\frac{1}{1}(-4x-0) \\\\  & =-4x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, we can conclude that an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int -4x\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-2{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand by multiplying our differential equation by the integrating factor, we have\n\n$$\nI(x)\\cdot (-(4xy+3x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=I(x)\\cdot 0\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n{e}^{-2{x}^{2}}\\cdot (-(4xy+3x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0.\n$$" 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311814 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311455 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311814 1069 "q-337164" 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311814 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311814 1071 "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(5,{10}^{2}),$ compute $P(-18.4<X<16.7).$\n\n| | $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.4\\,$ | $\\,0.0075\\,$ | $\\,0.0073\\,$ | $\\,0.0071\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0099\\,$ | $\\,0.0096\\,$ | $\\,0.0094\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.0129\\,$ | $\\,0.0125\\,$ | $\\,0.0122\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8577\\,$ | $\\,0.8599\\,$ | $\\,0.8621\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8790\\,$ | $\\,0.8810\\,$ | $\\,0.8830\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8980\\,$ | $\\,0.8997\\,$ | $\\,0.9015\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.4\\,$ | $\\,0.0075\\,$ | $\\,0.0073\\,$ | $\\,0.0071\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0099\\,$ | $\\,0.0096\\,$ | $\\,0.0094\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.0129\\,$ | $\\,0.0125\\,$ | $\\,0.0122\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n|