\\begin{aligned}4t{e}^{3t} \\\\ -t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}4t{e}^{3t} \\\\ -t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 4t{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int -t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=4t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=4\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4t{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(4t)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\int \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}t{e}^{3t}-\\frac{4}{3}\\int {e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}t{e}^{3t}-\\frac{4}{9}{e}^{3t} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{e}^{3t}(3t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=-t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=-\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v={e}^{t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(-t)\\cdot {e}^{t}-\\int {e}^{t}(-\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-t{e}^{t}+\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-t{e}^{t}+{e}^{t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(1-t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t} & 3{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{9}{e}^{3t}(3t-1) \\\\ {e}^{t}(1-t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}4(3t-1)+9(1-t) \\\\ 4(3t-1)+27(1-t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}3t+5 \\\\ 23-15t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311837 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311318 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311837 1069 "q-337287" 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311837 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533416 17592186045585 true] [17592186311837 1071 "